Alembic migrations for MarketEngine AI.

Generic single-database configuration with an async dbapi.

The database URL is not configured here or in alembic.ini -- env.py reads
DATABASE_URL from app.core.config.settings, the same value the application
uses. Set it in the repository-root .env file.

Run all commands from the backend/ directory:

    alembic upgrade head                          # apply migrations
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "message"  # create one after a model change
    alembic current                               # show the current revision
    alembic check                                 # detect model/database drift

For a database created before Alembic was introduced, see the "Existing
database" section in the baseline migration's docstring
(versions/63f75cc5fbb2_baseline.py) -- use `alembic stamp head`, not `upgrade`.

Full documentation: the "Database migrations" section of the root README.md.
